*
** Released by: Texas Instruments Inc.
* Part: LM73100
* Date: 11DEC2020
* Model Type: TRANSIENT
* Simulator: PSPICE
* Simulator Version: 17.2-2016 S067
* EVM Order Number: LM73100EVM
* EVM Users Guide: SNOU173 – OCTOBER 2020
* Datasheet: SNOSDC0 – OCTOBER 2020
*
* Model Version: Final 1.00
*
*****************************************************************************
*
* Updates:
*
* Final 1.00
* Release to Web.
*
*****************************************************************************
*
* Model Usage Notes:
* A. Features have been modelled
*	1. 	Startup
*	2. 	Switching charcteristics for different CdVdT
*	3. 	Reverse Current Blocking
*	4. 	Input Reverse Polarity Protection
*	5. 	Undervoltage Lockout (UVLO & UVP)
*	6. 	Overvoltage Lockout (OVLO)
*	7. 	Slew Rate (dVdt) and Inrush Current Control
*	8. 	Short-Circuit Protection
*	9. 	Analog Load Current Monitor
*	10. Fault Response (Latch-off)
*	11. Power Good Indication (PG)
*	12. Quiescent, shutdown current and Leakage current at IN and OUT 
*
* B. Features have not been modelled
*	1.  Temperature dependent characteristics are not modelled. Thermal Shutdown
*       Time vs Power Dissipation is modelled such that temperature is not taken  
*       into account and only Power dissipation vs shutdowndelay time is taken.
*       Once delay is hit a narrow pulse pulls down the gate resulting in shutdown.
*
*****************************************************************************
.SUBCKT LM73100_TRANS dVdt EN_UVLO GND IMON IN NC OUT OVLO PG PGTH PARAMS:
+  TA=25
